   <file>
   00001| The original self-coding and CI-audit sessions remain byte-exact. Their SHA-256 identities are pinned in `native-protocol-capture-provenance.json` and its closest JavaScript tests.
   00002| 
   00003| The two versioned captures are complete actual right-hand JSON operands emitted by native coverage tests on source `4a560cdb5a47dd3d175ca16adf6d521619437a4e`, tree `2ddcb2797fe522f4c9335e445d8d3c37e5406ba8`, run [37870721768](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/actions/runs/37870721768). The provenance contract records exact job IDs and raw log lines. Decoding the assertion's JSON string preserved every session field and byte; it did not normalize tool calls. The self-coding test trimmed its operand, so its observed capture has no terminal LF; the CI-audit test emitted one LF, which is preserved.
   00004| 
   00005| The original schema advertised five tools. Native CI advertised six, adding `read_file`; it observed plan-history reads and append semantics before the target write. The immutable first-write protocol is distinct from this actual current protocol. The versioned records preserve the five actual calls and six turns rather than pretending either protocol emitted the other's calls.
   00006| 
   00007| The template-comparison task was never reached after the diagnostic comparison panicked. Its current session is therefore explicitly missing. `capture-native-agentic-protocol.mjs` runs all three unchanged original tasks through the already-built, receipt-verified native CLI in CI and retains complete sessions, stdout, stderr and source/toolchain provenance before asserting completeness. It performs no compilation and does not manufacture a passing capture after a failed invocation. Import the actual next-head artifact before closing that missing comparison. No native capture was executed locally.
   00008| 
   
